1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,964
How does Hanzi Island schedule review?

2
00:00:04,275 --> 00:00:10,011
Characters don't just disappear. A few days later, the island brings them back for review.

3
00:00:11,530 --> 00:00:18,562
Review comes first each day. When there's more to review, there are fewer new characters, so nothing piles up.

4
00:00:18,787 --> 00:00:21,883
Open the parents' page to see the details.

5
00:00:22,915 --> 00:00:30,019
The island keeps 'recognized alone' and 'recognized with hints' separate. Needing a hint doesn't count as knowing it yet.

6
00:00:30,591 --> 00:00:36,663
And only recognizing it again on a different day counts as 'remembered'. The numbers stay honest.

7
00:00:37,739 --> 00:00:42,868
This is a practice record — not a test, and never a comparison with other kids.

8
00:00:42,918 --> 00:00:49,206
The address is on screen. Does your child remember characters a few days later? Let me know in the comments.

